{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And you shall eat and be satisfied</b> — and adjacent to it is 'and you forget,' etc., that one must mention the day of death in Grace after Meals. Therefore they instituted HaTov veHaMeitiv for the slain of Betar, who were given burial." "<b>And you shall eat</b> — 'and bless': this is Grace after Meals. And so too one must bless beforehand. That is, 'and you shall eat and be satisfied and bless' — already, for a person is forbidden to derive benefit from this world without a blessing, as stated: 'To YHWH the earth and its fullness.' But after he has blessed, it is his own, as stated: 'and the earth He gave to mankind.' And this I said: 'I said to YHWH, my Master, You are my goodness — apart from You' — since I have declared to YHWH, the goodness is not yours.'" "<b>And you shall eat</b> — in gematria this is בכזית."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:12.612371688Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}